        "original_id": "6dbb3d8f-695f-5962-9520-1852cf58fb1d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marge Simpson, Julie Kavner, Margaret Groening\n- Works: \"Good Night,\" \"The Tracey Ullman Show,\" \"The Simpsons 138th Episode Spectacular,\" The Simpsons Season 1 DVD set\n- Topics: character naming, voice acting, first appearances, re-airing, DVD releases\n\nFacts:\n- Marge Simpson first appeared on television in \"Good Night,\" a short from \"The Tracey Ullman Show,\" on April 19, 1987.\n- Marge Simpson is voiced by Julie Kavner.\n- The character Marge Simpson was named after Margaret Groening, the mother of her creator.\n- \"Good Night\" was later aired in its entirety in the episode \"The Simpsons 138th Episode Spectacular\" along with several other Ullman shorts.\n- \"Good Night\" is one of the few Ullman shorts released on DVD, and it was included in The Simpsons Season 1 DVD set.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "627e8705-ef70-5b44-b60f-43bf0afaf13a",
        "text": "Page: Marge Simpson. Sentence: She is voiced by Julie Kavner and first appeared on television in \"The Tracey Ullman Show\" short \"Good Night\" on April 19, 1987.\nPage: Marge Simpson. Sentence: He named the character after his mother Margaret Groening.\nPage: Good Night (The Simpsons short). Sentence: \"Good Night\" has since been aired on the show in the episode \"The Simpsons 138th Episode Spectacular\" (in its entirety), along with several other Ullman shorts, and is one of the few shorts to ever be released on DVD, being included in the Season 1 DVD set.",
